---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE } from "../data/site";

const updated = "2026-10-12";
---

<Base
  title={`Privacy · ${SITE.name}`}
  description="What Karakoa collects when you use this site or send an inquiry, and how it is used."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-5 pb-20 sm:px-6">
    <header class="pb-8 pt-14 sm:pt-20">
      <p class="reveal eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1 class="reveal d1 mt-4 text-title1 font-semibold text-ink sm:text-large">How we handle your details</h1>
      <p class="reveal d2 mt-3 text-footnote text-muted">Last updated {updated}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="reveal d2 prose">
      <p>
        This site is a static website. It sets no cookies and loads no advertising or tracking
        scripts. Fonts and images are served from this domain.
      </p>

      <h2>The inquiry form</h2>
      <p>
        When you send the form, the details you enter (your name, email, what you need, project size,
        timeline, and message) are delivered by <a href="https://web3forms.com" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Web3Forms</a>
        to our inbox. Web3Forms passes the message on and keeps it only for delivery. We use your details to
        reply to you and, if you go ahead with a project, to work with you. We do not sell or share them.
      </p>

      <h2>Direct channels</h2>
      <p>
        Email and Calendly links open those services. Each one has its own privacy policy
        that applies when you use it.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The site is served by Cloudflare, which keeps standard request logs (such as IP address and
        request time) for security and performance, and measures page speed with its cookieless
        real user monitoring beacon. Neither identifies you to us, and we add no tracking of our own.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        Ask us to delete any inquiry you sent and we will. Write to
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
